    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>Sara Anne Winder, firstborn of English nobleman Roger Winder, was educated as a man's equal and graduated (secretly, as a woman) from Oxford with honors before the university revoked her degree upon discovering the deception. Embraced by the Ventrue elder Charlotte Ingraham after two years of cultivation, Winder became a strong proponent of Camarilla ideals and rose to prominence as one of the strategists behind the reconquest of New York City. That success won her the Inner Circle's blessing to become Prince of San Francisco &mdash; on the condition she first retake the city from the Kuei-jin who seized it from her predecessor, Jochen Van Nuys.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>Winder is a battle-hardened general in the guise of a sweet, flirtatious young woman: gracious even to enemies, willing to use any tactic to win, but never gratuitously cruel. She waits on Inner Circle authorization for a mass-Embrace campaign to retake the city outright, relying in the meantime on agents like Kelvin Wee, her bodyguard Miriam Caravaggio, and the loyalty of Kokopell Mana and Luna Demian.</p>",
    "notes": "Sire: Charlotte Ingraham. Bodyguard: Miriam Caravaggio (Toreador). Key allies: Kokopell Mana (Nosferatu primogen), Luna Demian (Tremere Regent), Kelvin Wee (Camarilla negotiator with the Mandarinate). Disciplines (as printed): Auspex 2, Celerity 4, Dominate 5, Fortitude 4, Potence 2, Presence 5.",
    "npcType": "vampire"
  },
